UDP dispatcher: make connEntry.closed atomic, so terminate no longer races the dispatches that read it

Upstream: b1905088c3195992c345dfd35d2fbef515c3bd49

terminate runs on the inactivity timer's goroutine and wrote connEntry.closed while getInboundRay
read it under the dispatcher lock, which terminate does not take: a data race whenever the timer
ends a flow while a packet for its destination is being dispatched. Upstream #7411 makes closed an atomic.Bool and logs a
read failure after a local termination at debug level instead of info. The change in
transport/internet/udp/dispatcher.go is upstream's, unchanged; the file is identical at the pin and
at the upstream commit's parent. transport/internet/udp/dispatcher_close_race_test.go is fork code:
four goroutines dispatch to a destination whose link refuses writes, so every dispatch closes its
flow and the next one reads closed while the timer terminates it.

